# sweep: --seed-root apps/readeck/fixtures/kept
# A Readeck account with the last inbox kept on the reader and one article
# kept from an earlier read. The sweep has no Readeck server, so this is a
# reader away from home: the kept inbox stays on screen under a banner that
# says why, the kept article reads to its end, and every change or search
# says the server did not answer instead of pretending.
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
expect Try again
expect A morning at the river
expect A morning at the harbour
clean
shot inbox-kept
# The kept inbox pages to its last article.
page next
page next
page next
page next
wait-for A morning at the bridge
clean
shot inbox-last-page
# The page key turns back; on the first page it stays put.
page back
page back
page back
page back
wait-for A morning at the harbour
# The harbour article was opened before, so it opens without the server and
# reads to its last line.
tap A morning at the harbour
wait-for-id reader-forward
wait-idle
expect A morning at the harbour
expect Paragraph 1.
clean
shot article-first-page
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
tap-id reader-forward
wait-idle
expect The end of the walk.
clean
shot article-end
# The middle of the page opens the article's controls. A change needs the
# server, so it says the server did not answer and keeps the article.
tap-id reader-controls
wait-for Article controls
expect Mark read
expect Archive
expect Unfavorite
expect Delete article
clean
shot controls
tap Delete article
wait-for Delete this article?
expect This removes it from your Readeck library.
clean
shot delete-confirm
tap Keep article
wait-for Article controls
tap Mark read
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
expect Continue
clean
shot change-refused
tap Continue
wait-for Article controls
tap Return to article
wait-for-id reader-forward
expect The end of the walk.
# Back keeps the place: the article reopens on its last page, and so it
# does after a restart.
tap Back
wait-for A morning at the harbour
tap A morning at the harbour
wait-for-id reader-forward
wait-idle
expect The end of the walk.
tap Back
wait-for A morning at the harbour
restart
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
tap A morning at the harbour
wait-for-id reader-forward
wait-idle
expect The end of the walk.
tap Back
wait-for A morning at the harbour
# Search needs the server too, and says so; Back returns to the kept inbox.
tap Search
wait-for Search terms
expect Search includes read and archived articles.
type river
tap Search
wait 10000
wait-for did not answer
expect Search: river
clean
shot search-refused
tap Back
wait 10000
wait-for A morning at the harbour
# More holds Refresh and the account, which opens on the saved address.
tap More
wait-for Refresh
expect Account
clean
shot more
tap Account
wait-for Connect Readeck
expect https://127.0.0.1:47444
expect Use saved token
clean
shot account
tap Back
wait 10000
wait-for A morning at the harbour
# The inbox says which page of how many it is on, as every paged list does.
expect 1 of
